  "solution": {
    "text": "We can re-write the equation of the curve as<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8901;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>c</mi></msup><mo>&#8901;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />or <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8901;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> (where,&nbsp;<math><mi>k</mi></math> is an arbitrary constant)<br />As there are <math><mi>&#8216;</mi><mn>4</mn><mi>&#8217;</mi></math> such constants, hence the order of the differential equation will be <math><mi>&#8216;</mi><mn>4</mn><mi>&#8217;</mi></math>",
